# The commit of qoryai/forager whose contracts/forager/v1 the :contract tests replay, in
# CI and in development (Apiary.ContractFixtures.contract_dir/0): a commit of Forager
# after its release v0.7.0, pinned by its id, where an enrolment code's
# prefix names its node's kind (`qec[npgi]_`): Forager's module in three parts over one
# core, the session, the gateway and the wall, with a gateway between the session and
# Qory Apiary, every run's exit saying how the run ended, discovery listing the one
# workspace an access key's node or node pool belongs to, and a run that goes through a
# gateway: the run key, the registration's gateway shape, the attach, the outcome and
# the end member, a gateway's key in discovery and enrolment, a gateway's enrolment
# request and its signed answer, a gateway's discovery document without workspaces, and
# the refusals of a gateway that may no longer serve a run's workspace; a run
# configuration and a policy may name the image by a reference pinned by digest, and
# Forager's deny list leaves in the server's values of QORY_RUN_SYSTEM and
# QORY_RUN_REPOSITORIES; the fixed list of model API formats (api-format.schema.json),
# and a runtime's `model` in runtimes.json, with the formats it sends; a run
# configuration's `credentials`, whose values the server seals to the access key in its
# answer to the secrets request, a signed POST to discovery's `secrets.url`; a Claude
# Code runtime that requires no model key; a gateway that opens its machine only for an
# exact entry of the node's policy, never for an entry of a server's policy; a runtime's
# `model.keys`, the variables it reads a model key from, each for one API format and
# auth, an OAuth token marked `oauth`; the sealed answer to the secrets request, with
# its known answers under fixtures/sealed; and a policy's `egress.allow_first`, at most
# 64 exact hosts that the gateway allows before `deny` and `allow`; the 13 event types
# that a runtime descriptor produces, each `dev.qory.runtime.<name>`; and a run split
# from its sessions: `dev.qory.run.started` with `opened_by` `run` and no runtime
# members, a `dev.qory.session.started` with the runtime members and a
# `dev.qory.session.exited` for each session, numbered from 1, and the
# `dev.qory.run.exited` reason `no_session`, a run closed with no session started; and a
# wall that refuses a session after its `dev.qory.session.started`, whose
# `dev.qory.session.exited` has the refusal's code as its reason; `session`, the
# session's number, on each `dev.qory.run.log`, `dev.qory.run.resized` and runtime event
# of a session, and no `image_fetch_ms` on `dev.qory.session.started`; and the steps of
# a run's host work and joins, each a `dev.qory.run.step_started` and a
# `dev.qory.run.step_exited` numbered from 1, with `step` on each `dev.qory.run.log` of
# a step; and a run code, `qecr_`, which a machine redeems once at enrolment for its
# run's run key, answered `$defs/run_answer` of `enrolment.schema.json`, with the run's
# `documents`; and `machine` and `setup`, optional members of `dev.qory.run.started`;
# and a run key's `gateway_url` of `https://`, a host and an optional port alone, at
# most 300 characters; and a gateway's relay that signs a run code's enrolment as the
# gateway, `qory-request-ed25519-v1`, over the raw body, with no timestamp header; and
# `environment_image` and `base`, optional members of `dev.qory.run.built`, the
# environment image and the base image by their digests; and `(a name that contains a
# run code)` and `(a value that contains a run code)`, the phrases in place of a name or
# a value that contains `qecr_` and neither `qak_` nor `qrk_`; and `stack_proxy_secret`,
# a member of `link-run-answer` on the local link alone, which a `link-reload-answer`
# must not contain; and a run with a run key, whose `dev.qory.run.started` has no
# `host`, whose `dev.qory.session.started` has `dir` `/workspace` and no `harness`, and
# whose `command`, `args`, `cwd` and `prompt` have `<run>`, `<home>` and `<inputs>` in
# place of the run directory, the harness home and the inputs directory, and whose `cwd`
# and `prompt` have `/workspace` in place of the working directory; and `qecr_` in the
# strings for which `(*session.Run).Built` returns an error, in any case, in the image
# and in `environment_image` and `base` of `dev.qory.run.built`; and `setup` of
# `dev.qory.run.started`, where the run's setup commands run, or would run if it had
# any, absent when the run has nowhere to run setup commands; and `runner` `true` on the
# `line` event of a setup record, written by the runner when it cannot start or wait for
# the command; and the line `session <n> starts on this machine`, which the session
# reports on stderr by default, with the host, the directories on the machine, the
# command and the arguments, and the harness sources that a run with a run key leaves
# out of its events or replaces; and `(a name that contains an enrolment code)` and `(a
# value that contains an enrolment code)`, the phrases in place of a name or a value
# that contains `qecn_`, `qecp_`, `qecg_` or `qeci_`, in any case, and none of `qak_`,
# `qrk_` and `qecr_`, in the 7 event schemas that have the other phrases; and those four
# prefixes in the strings for which `(*session.Run).Built` returns an error; and a host
# credential's `apply` items, each with its hosts, scheme and paths, in place of its
# `hosts`, `paths` and `auth`, and its `purpose`, `work` or `harness`; a sealed value's
# `expires_at` and `apply`, and a secrets request at a renewal for the entries that are
# due; and a run configuration's `stack_hosts` and `harness_hidden`, and `channel`
# `stack` on the stack proxy's `dev.qory.run.egress`.
#
